.TH SYMPY_CALC 1 "2026-06-29" "Symoneural" "Symoneural Helper Utilities"
.SH NAME
sympy_calc \- SymPy-based calculus engine (derivatives, integrals, limits, ODEs, numeric)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python helpers/python/sympy_calc.py
.I MODE
.I EXPR
.RB [ \-\-var
.IR VAR ]
.RB [ \-\-order
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-lower
.IR L ]
.RB [ \-\-upper
.IR U ]
.RB [ \-\-point
.IR P ]
.RB [ \-\-direction
.BR + | \- | +\- ]
.RB [ \-\-func
.IR F ]
.RB [ \-\-precision
.IR N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sympy_calc.py
evaluates a mathematical expression using the SymPy symbolic mathematics
library and returns LaTeX output, a numeric approximation, and a SymPy
string representation.  It is also the engine behind the
.B /api/calc
backend endpoint.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B derivative
Compute the n-th derivative of
.I EXPR
with respect to
.IR VAR .
.TP
.B integral
Compute the indefinite or definite integral of
.I EXPR .
Specify
.B \-\-lower
and
.B \-\-upper
for a definite integral.
.TP
.B limit
Compute
.RI lim_{ VAR \→ P }
.I EXPR .
Use
.B \-\-direction
to control one-sided vs two-sided limit.
.TP
.B ode
Solve an ordinary differential equation expressed as a SymPy expression.
The equation is assumed equal to zero unless wrapped with
.BR Eq() .
.TP
.B numeric
Numerically evaluate
.I EXPR
to
.I N
significant digits after substituting any variable values.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-var \fIVAR\fR
Variable name (default:
.BR x ).
.TP
.B \-\-order \fIN\fR
Derivative order (default:
.BR 1 ).
.TP
.B \-\-lower \fIL\fR
Lower bound for definite integrals.
.TP
.B \-\-upper \fIU\fR
Upper bound for definite integrals.
.TP
.B \-\-point \fIP\fR
Limit point (default:
.BR 0 ).
Use
.B oo
for infinity.
.TP
.B \-\-direction \fI{+,-,+-}\fR
Limit direction (default:
.BR + ).
.TP
.B \-\-func \fIF\fR
Dependent function name for ODE mode (default:
.BR y ).
.TP
.B \-\-precision \fIN\fR
Numeric precision in significant digits (default:
.BR 15 ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Second derivative:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/sympy_calc.py derivative "x**4 - 3*x**2 + 1" \-\-order 2
.EE
.RE
.PP
Definite integral from 0 to π:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/sympy_calc.py integral "sin(x)" \-\-lower 0 \-\-upper pi
.EE
.RE
.PP
Two-sided limit at 0:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/sympy_calc.py limit "sin(x)/x" \-\-point 0 \-\-direction +-
.EE
.RE
.PP
Solve ODE y' + y = x:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/sympy_calc.py ode "y(x).diff(x) + y(x) - x"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Evaluate to 30 digits:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/sympy_calc.py numeric "sqrt(2) + pi" \-\-precision 30
.EE
.RE
.SH OUTPUT
JSON object with keys:
.TP
.B latex
LaTeX-rendered result string.
.TP
.B numeric
Decimal approximation string (empty for indefinite integrals).
.TP
.B expr
SymPy string representation.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B sympy
(pip install sympy).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tensor_utils (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Symoneural contributors.
